      "kind": "recomp",
      "game": "super-mario-bros-wonder",
      "developer": "seedds",
      "summary": "Super Mario Bros. Wonder’s own code, running natively on the Mac.",
      "description": "nxnative runs a Switch game’s own arm64 code natively: it rewrites the game’s code modules so they run outside a Switch, stands in for the Switch’s system with a host of its own, and translates the game’s NVN graphics and shaders to Metal. Upstream makes iPhone and iPad apps; on the Mac it has a development host, which Frontport builds from source and wraps in an app. The build reads your NSPs (or NSZs) and console keys and makes the game files the app plays from. Settings such as the game language go in env.txt in the Port’s Data, one DM_ setting per line.\n\nIt plays version 1.2.1, the one upstream brought it up on, so it needs the base game and the 1.2.1 update. Upstream notes that on the Mac the menus’ and dialogue’s text are blank, though they show on an iPhone.",
      "source": "https://github.com/seedds/nxnative",
      "bundleId": "dev.frontport.port.nxnative-wonder",
