    {
      "id": "macnativegames-totk",
      "name": "MacNativeGames",
      "kind": "recomp",
      "game": "tears-of-the-kingdom",
      "developer": "ly05010419",
      "summary": "Tears of the Kingdom’s own code on the Mac, its graphics rebuilt on Metal.",
      "description": "MacNativeGames runs a Switch game’s own arm64 code natively: it rewrites the game’s code modules for Apple silicon, answers the Switch’s system services with a small host, and rebuilds the game’s NVN graphics on Metal. Upstream builds a Mac app on your Mac from your own files; Frontport builds that app from source. The build reads your NSPs, console keys and a Switch firmware, whose shared fonts the game uses, and compiles every startup shader ahead, so the game doesn’t stop to compile them; the first start still builds its render pipelines before the title, which takes minutes once.\n\nIt plays version 1.4.3, so it needs the base game and the 1.4.3 update. Key 1 opens its settings: a frame rate lock, MetalFX upscaling and frame interpolation, resolutions up to 2K, ultrawide aspect ratios and mouse aiming.",
      "source": "https://github.com/ly05010419/MacNativeGames",
      "bundleId": "dev.frontport.port.macnativegames-totk",
